(# Distilling a coding fleet into a small self-hosted model) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Paul B. Isaac's | Rust assessment design v1.1 | 15 October 2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Status: frozen before assessment implementation at the real timestamp in docs/design-freeze.txt. No calls,) Tj T*
(checkpoint, improvement or measured cost is claimed. Original repository history is preserved; subsequent changes go) Tj T*
(in docs/deviations.md.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## 1. The loop and its ceiling) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Versioned tasks -> configurable teacher fleet -> isolated execution and grading -> eligible, deduplicated training) Tj T*
(examples -> adapter checkpoint -> held-out gate -> local canary -> new tasks and verified failures. Selection) Tj T*
(records which output won and why; only passing, rights-cleared training-source outputs enter supervised fine-tuning) Tj T*
(\(SFT\). Serving logs replenish the development queue, never the sealed assessment set.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The student can exceed an individual teacher's pass@1 on a narrow distribution by learning complementary verified) Tj T*
(solutions, reducing avoidable errors and specialising. It may also outperform a finite fleet sample on unseen tasks) Tj T*
(through generalisation and its existing pretraining; this is a hypothesis, not a guaranteed outcome. The observed) Tj T*
(best-of-three candidate set is a reference point, not a universal theoretical upper bound. Distillation alone) Tj T*
(supplies no verified corrective answer for an item on which every candidate fails. Verifiers, new tasks or search) Tj T*
(add signal. There is no credible claim of generally surpassing frontier capability from this small round; the) Tj T*
(commercial aim is cheaper verified success at comparable quality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## 2. Task supply and clean separation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Start with 96 short Rust function tasks from 24 locally authored private specification/source packs: 12 packs/48) Tj T*
(tasks train, four/16 development, eight/32 sealed test. Assign complete packs before provider calls. A shared) Tj T*
(generator, repository ancestor or specification template is one source; changing inputs or seeds never creates a new) Tj T*
(source. Commit task, oracle, author, creation time and lineage hashes. Sources share AI authorship; source) Tj T*
(independence and algorithmic novelty remain limitations. Teachers receive specifications and public examples, never) Tj T*
(hidden tests or oracle code. Test outputs are evaluation-only.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For a week, ingest rights-cleared issue fixes from consenting private repositories and independently authored) Tj T*
(contracts, then add oracle-backed boundary cases and mutations within existing splits. Track source diversity, not) Tj T*
(only sample count. New source packs, human verification of ambiguous contracts, and budget determine replenishment.) Tj T*
(Public benchmarks remain diagnostic: new random inputs do not erase exposure to a public problem. Private provenance) Tj T*
(reduces contamination risk; it cannot prove that no model has seen equivalent algorithms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## 3. Grading, cheapest first) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reject empty, truncated or unparsable responses; enforce the function interface and output schema. Next check) Tj T*
(forbidden operations and obvious harness tampering. Static checks can miss aliases and reject legitimate code: they) Tj T*
(are a fast filter, never the security boundary. Run public examples, then hidden edge/property tests and) Tj T*
(differential checks against an independently reviewed oracle. Public-example hardcoding is caught by fresh private) Tj T*
(inputs; correlated oracle bugs need a second implementation or manual review. Unresolved specifications are) Tj T*
(quarantined.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A trusted Rust controller owns expected answers, case count and verdicts outside the candidate container. Candidate) Tj T*
(stdout, exit status, test-like JSON or 'all passed' text cannot grant success. Every required response must arrive) Tj T*
(with the right schema; timeout, crash, early exit or missing output is failure. Hidden inputs necessarily reach the) Tj T*
(candidate, but hidden test code and answers do not. Host-owned syscall traces record denied network/file probes; any) Tj T*
(prohibited attempt scores zero and is quarantined, even if caught by the program. Bound inputs, output, CPU, memory) Tj T*
(and trace volume. The extra property runs and tracing cost CPU; skip expensive layers after a definitive failure. A) Tj T*
(hash of every grader version accompanies each score.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
