(## 4. Interaction and training) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Baseline: one independent completion from each of three provider businesses, then choose a fully passing candidate,) Tj T*
(breaking ties by measured cost and output length. Config carries endpoint, model/revision, rate limits, token) Tj T*
(ceilings, prices and output-training permissions. Rejection sampling SFT learns the selected solution; selection) Tj T*
(reasons and rejected runs remain auditable. No passing candidate means no positive example. Save preference pairs) Tj T*
(for later; do not add DPO or online RL with this small, noisy dataset.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An optional critique experiment runs only on development sources: compare three independent calls with proposal ->) Tj T*
(critique -> revision under identical per-task dollar ceilings, including critic context, reasoning tokens, retries) Tj T*
(and grading. Run both arms on matched tasks in randomised order; compare paired verified success and cost, with) Tj T*
(intervals. Its possible benefit is repairing complementary errors; its risks are correlated mistakes, prompt) Tj T*
(injection and extra latency. Keep best-of-three unless the priced experiment justifies changing it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Adapt Apache-2.0 Qwen2.5-Coder-0.5B-Instruct [1] with native Rust Candle LoRA, rank 8, assistant-token-only loss,) Tj T*
(short sequences and a development-selected fixed schedule. Use CPU float32 initially; the observed RTX 2080 has 8) Tj T*
(GiB and GPU use requires a real smoke test. Measure CPU time. Train a second seed-control adapter with identical) Tj T*
(data/hyperparameters. Store base revision, tokenizer/chat template, dataset hash, seed, optimiser steps,) Tj T*
(changed-weight hashes and reload/inference evidence. These criteria survive roster changes: open runnable weights,) Tj T*
(licence compatibility, task fit, memory, stable tooling and measurable quality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Terms are an eligibility constraint, not an inference from output ownership. DeepSeek's API terms explicitly permit) Tj T*
(training/distillation [2]. Together's terms assign outputs but require compliance with each hosted model's terms) Tj T*
([3]. Mistral's reviewed commercial/additional terms make text output a candidate, subject to selected model/account) Tj T*
(terms [4]. Anthropic and Gemini restrict competing-model development [5,6]. Enable three providers only after) Tj T*
(retaining applicable terms/licences and a dated permission decision; ambiguous material cannot enter training. Do) Tj T*
(not bypass a provider restriction through another host.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## 5. Proof of learning and the gate) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Select all hyperparameters and the candidate on development sources. Freeze the candidate, evaluation seeds and ship) Tj T*
(margin before opening test results. Evaluate incumbent and candidate on identical inputs, decoding settings and) Tj T*
(grader versions; count every failed generation in the denominator. Primary metric: source-macro average of task) Tj T*
(success across three predeclared decoding seeds. Tests and seeds are repeated observations, not extra independent) Tj T*
(tasks. Report individual teachers and fleet best-of-three descriptively; no post-hoc 'best teacher' significance) Tj T*
(claim.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Let each held-out source contribute one paired mean difference. Report the mean and a two-sided 95% source-level t) Tj T*
(interval, explicitly assuming approximately independent source effects and an adequate t approximation; provide a) Tj T*
(source-cluster bootstrap sensitivity interval. Eight sources are weak evidence. Ship only if both intervals' lower) Tj T*
(bounds exceed +2 percentage points, all security checks pass, and every task/seed is accounted for. Otherwise say NO) Tj T*
(SHIP with regression, inconclusive or invalid-evaluation reason. A predeclared non-regression slice is an additional) Tj T*
(block, never an alternative route to shipping. Use a fresh sealed set or a predeclared alpha budget for later) Tj T*
(candidates.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Report 80%-power minimum detectable effect \(MDE\) from simulations of this exact rule, using development-estimated) Tj T*
(discordance, clustering and seed variance, with sensitivity ranges. Sanity check: with 32 independent binary task) Tj T*
(pairs, discordance q=0.30 and a two-sided 5% test, normal MDE is about 27.1 points; clustering can worsen it. This) Tj T*
(is not the gate's final MDE. A few extra passes or a seed-only difference is not proof; a seed-only comparison can) Tj T*
(occasionally be significant by chance. Label drill fixtures separately from actual checkpoint comparisons.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
